From: Jinbo Zhang <jinboz1@uci.edu>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 17:23:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] Flatten event_id before naming or saving stage outputs

Each stage that batches events through a DataLoader wraps the string
event_id in another list, and several savers index it with [0]. After
metric learning -> GNN -> track building, outputs were written as
event['000021009'].pyg.gz, which also breaks subdir_size sharding
(_shard_path cannot parse the id). If the id was already a plain string,
event_id[0] silently took its first character.

Add loading_utils.flatten_event_id (unwraps any list/tuple nesting,
rejects multi-event containers), use it wherever an output file name is
built (metric learning, edge classifier, track-building stage,
walkthrough), and store the flat id in the saved graph.

gd-displaced patch 0005 (plan item e).
